From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:34:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 220/221] fix(area): water rebuilds from current points after a
 pivot recenter

Recenter Pivot on a polygon carrying Water Volume left the outline where it was
and translated the water by the pivot delta, keeping its shape.

Area water's node geometry is LOCAL, relative to contour point 0, and the entity
slot's local transform carries that point (m_localOrigin) so that the fog plane
lands where the legacy object puts it. Recenter Pivot moves the entity AND
rewrites every local point to compensate, so the WORLD contour never changes -
only the entity-space one does. The component treated a transform notification as
"move the physics area, nothing else", never re-read the points, and kept an
origin belonging to the old pivot: node matrix = new entity transform x old
origin, which is the observed translation exactly.

Three changes, any one of which would have been enough, kept together because the
notification order here is not something to rely on:

- every OnShapeChanged reason now goes through the rebuild digest, transforms
  included. Area water's digest is taken in entity space, so dragging the entity
  still costs nothing and the matrix-only move decision 05 promised is intact;
- before the digest, a rebuild is forced when the contour's first point in entity
  space has drifted from m_localOrigin. That is the recenter case named directly,
  and it survives any order the notifications arrive in;
- the component now also listens to ENTITY_EVENT_XFORM itself, as insurance for
  the case where it was not yet bound to the shape when the entity moved.

RebuildIfNeeded returns whether it rebuilt, so the transform path still moves the
physics area by hand when it did not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
